  "data": {
    "body": "A \\textbf{spherical} toy has mass M = \\textbf{0.6 kg} and radius R = \\textbf{0.1 m}. A string is wrapped around the toy and the other end of the string is attached to the ceiling. The toy is suspended from the ceiling with this string and then let go from rest, with the string vertical. The spherical toy rotates as it moves vertically downward with the string unwinding around it's circumference without slipping. \n\nWhat is the \\textbf{angular speed}, $\\omega$ of the rotating spherical toy after it has fallen a vertical distance \\textbf{h = 0.9 m}? \\textbf{Select the closest answer.}\n\nAssume that the magnitude of acceleration due to gravity is g = 10 m/s$^2$.\n\nMoment of inertia of the \\textbf{spherical toy} is \\textbf{I} = $\\frac{2}{5} MR^2$",
